Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.04,0:00:04.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, welcome everyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.62,0:00:11.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this is the keynote session uh robot learning and models and it is my great pleasure to be the chairman of this session.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.45,0:00:15.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,My name is Karinne Ramirez-Amaro and I'm an associate professor at Chalmers University of
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.59,0:00:20.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Technology in Sweden and it's my great pleasure to introduce our first speaker uh David Hsu.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.92,0:00:28.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,David is a provost chair professor in the department of computer science at the national university of Singapore.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.11,0:00:34.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,He's also the director of NVIDIA Research Lab in Singapore and he is an IEEE Fellow and of course has
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.70,0:00:43.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,won multiple awards for example the test time award at RSS in 2021 and the IJCAI-JAIR Best Paper Prize in 2022.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.42,0:00:50.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,So without further notice I I will give you the award.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.56,0:00:53.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, right.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.86,0:00:56.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,It is a really exciting time for robotics, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.43,0:01:04.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we have massive amount of compute and data and the foundation models have brought in a new age of robotics research, technology and the industry.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.99,0:01:10.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh now against this exciting background, I want to ask a very basic and hopefully important question.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.88,0:01:15.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Have we solved the problem of robot decision- making in the open world?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.76,0:01:17.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so what's the open world?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.48,0:01:22.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, imagine that we have we unbox a home service robot in a new home.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.10,0:01:25.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,This robot has been trained in the factory on a variety of different kind of home but it
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.84,0:01:32.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,has never met seen this home and this robot is equipped with an RGBD camera or other sensors.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.28,0:01:42.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,It is pre-trained with some scales to pick up and place objects to open and close doors etc etc. it has access to uh foundation models,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.46,0:01:46.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,lms, VLMs or whatever the latest variety is.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.56,0:01:54.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh to make this really concrete, maybe all we wanted the robot to do is to operate the variety of different home appliances at home.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.36,0:01:58.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And in my view, the challenge remains in the open world.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.48,0:02:00.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,There are two two of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.17,0:02:02.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,The first one is the scalability.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.49,0:02:05.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have many different kind of home appliances.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.26,0:02:07.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,Each of them can be fairly complex.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.65,0:02:12.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,And second, any of those appliance may be new to our robot and it doesn't know what to do about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.87,0:02:14.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,So there's uncertainty.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.04,0:02:18.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,So what ideas do we have to address these two challenges?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.93,0:02:23.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,In the abstract, we can think of our robot as a function.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.20,0:02:30.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's just a box that maps a history of perceptual inputs to output and action for robot execution.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.88,0:02:36.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now in the classic era of uh robotics, it's primarily model-based.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.30,0:02:39.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,We think of this box consisting of modules.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.79,0:02:44.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Modules for perception, state estimation, planning and control.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.19,0:02:52.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Within each of module, we have models for system dynamics, for sensor observations, for task objectives.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.42,0:02:58.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,We reason over these models in order to derive the desirable robot behavior.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.24,0:03:03.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,This uh model-based approach has a distinguished and long record.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.26,0:03:06.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Most celebrated robots are built this way.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.24,0:03:08.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Shakey, the very first robot system.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.96,0:03:14.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,Stanley, the one that opened up the autonomous driving industry.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.18,0:03:22.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,In fact, most of the engineering systems that we experience in our daily life is built this way.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.16,0:03:32.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, the biggest challenge to this model based um approach in practice is how do we acquire good models, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.88,0:03:38.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh a little bit less than uh a decade ago and there came the deep learning era.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.47,0:03:41.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,Deep learning era is datadriven.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.05,0:03:46.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,We think of this box uh we put in this box uh single monolithic uh
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.91,0:03:53.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,neural network and we acquire massive amount of data to train this neural network control policy.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.86,0:04:01.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this approach although very sounds very simple has achieved enormous proc uh pro uh success on some of the
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.28,0:04:08.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,most challenging tasks that the model based approach have difficulty with right at the same time I think we should probably
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.96,0:04:18.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,um take the uh experimental evidence holistically despite the success of this datadriven approach probably I'm not aware of a
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.86,0:04:25.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh aircraft autopilot implemented this way uh if there is one and please Now let me know which airlines flying that.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.93,0:04:30.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm not going to get get onto the airplane again with that airline.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.64,0:04:39.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um more technically uh if we have trained such a neural network controller what if we
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.10,0:04:45.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,change something we change the robot we change a sensor or maybe just change a sensor mounting.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.68,0:04:54.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh what do we usually do and how do we generalize generals over different tasks, environment conditions and sometimes robot embodiment.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.08,0:04:59.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,So the key question over here is can we generalize?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.36,0:05:02.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Here comes now the foundation model.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.32,0:05:06.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,Foundation model brings us um a lot lot more interesting choices.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.04,0:05:13.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,We actually have to lay out our strategy over a two-dimensional space.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.16,0:05:17.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,The first one is how do we represent information?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.20,0:05:27.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,We can represent uh task relevant information in an unstructured manner as sequence of raw text, images or tokenized version of that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.73,0:05:34.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,At the other end, we can have structured representation as a list of objects, scene graphs and so on so forth.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.52,0:05:39.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And similarly in the other direction dimension, we have reasoning mechanisms.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.92,0:05:45.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have structured reasoning mechanisms which we systematically reason through
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.21,0:05:50.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,combinations of information by searching a tree or perform dynamic programming.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.82,0:05:57.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,We call this I call this planning or alternatively at the other end we can perform
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.96,0:06:08.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,autoregressive uh token prediction basically token concatenation I call that plan prediction planning and plant
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.24,0:06:15.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,prediction sometimes can generate the similar results however they are different the underlying um mechanism for
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.48,0:06:21.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,generating these results are different even though that the results sometimes are very similar or the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.72,0:06:27.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,So all the on the lower left quadrant we basically have the classic error the model based reasoning and
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.66,0:06:34.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,planning we have states base search first order logic MDP so on so forth right and they are um
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.72,0:06:45.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,compact efficient very precise but mostly close because of the model assumptions on the upper right quadrant uh we
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.11,0:06:53.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,can use the LLMs/VLMs simply as a policy we feed in the input and just ask the models
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.04,0:07:01.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,what should I do next right so it's definitely not compact it sometimes hallucinates but it's very expressive it
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.12,0:07:08.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,has no difficulty with open world at the cost of course sometimes hallucination in my view what's most interesting
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.92,0:07:18.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,the other remaining quadrants on the lower right even though we represent uh information in an unstructured manner we
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.08,0:07:24.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,structure the inference mechanism as a linear chain chain of thought as a table as a tree or graph.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.73,0:07:28.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now the upper left quadrant even more interesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.77,0:07:36.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,It says that we have structured the representation and then we ask the large model to predict what is the action to perform.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.79,0:07:44.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you come from a reasoning or planning background, this will be a very strange combination because if we had the structural representation,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.54,0:07:48.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,why don't we perform structured inference that should give us better results?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.94,0:07:51.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's a very interesting um question.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.52,0:07:58.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now one reason could be maybe that uh the answer uh the output is actually very simple is easy to learn.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.88,0:08:02.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,It does not require sophisticated the reasoning.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.30,0:08:02.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.74,0:08:08.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now let's uh now for this talk mostly I'm going to focus on the left two quadrants and
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.12,0:08:18.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,show that the structured information representation benefits both plan prediction and planning with the help of foundation models.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.48,0:08:25.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now let's look at uh first of all the robot operating home app appliances.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.12,0:08:30.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,So model home appliances can have a very complex uh control
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.31,0:08:35.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,panel with underlying partially observable mechanism right that's why it comes on manual
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.84,0:08:43.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,so the manual contains two kinds of things one is basically uh partial policies it tells us if you want to do this here are
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.54,0:08:51.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,the number of steps of actions the other one is system dynamics if I do this here are the consequences right now with that one
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.57,0:08:59.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,strategy is simply to condition the foundation model on the manual uh a PDF file and ask it to tell us what to do next.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.00,0:09:01.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,Alternatively,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.29,0:09:07.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,we may want to extract structured appliance model appliance model from this manual
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.79,0:09:12.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,and then condition the model on this structured information and do the plan prediction
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.93,0:09:16.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,a little bit more precisely that we're going to using the foundation model
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.26,0:09:21.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,to extract an appliance model consist of a state actions and and transition dynamics.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.70,0:09:22.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Basically,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.51,0:09:28.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's a factor the finance data model and we also extract macro actions in order to
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.06,0:09:37.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,act precisely to adjust certain variables very precisely through multiple se uh multiple uh repeated actions deterministically.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.70,0:09:41.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,For example, set the temperature to 85 degrees exactly, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.42,0:09:48.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,And with that and then at a deployment time the user gives a natural language instruction and we look at
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.25,0:09:56.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,the control panel visually and then condition all this information the language model will give us uh the next action.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.72,0:10:00.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so let's look at the some of the robot experiments.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.57,0:10:06.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,So for our robots you know operate a blender induction cooker and the water dispenser right.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.70,0:10:07.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.09,0:10:11.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,So let's look at the induction cooker a little bit more carefully that it's going to set it to
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.93,0:10:21.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,the hot spot hot pot mode and set a power to exactly 1600 uh 1600 watts for boiling the water.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.60,0:10:30.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right now looking more closely into the performance details or we primary want to compare uh the
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.09,0:10:36.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,benefits of the structured information in our approach versus if you just look query the foundation model directly.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.92,0:10:43.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,It should the performance should be the the the chart is clear that structured information representation enhances
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.02,0:10:50.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,performance for um plan production over a wider variety of home appliances that we tested in simulation.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.77,0:10:51.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.15,0:10:58.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Further this benefits expands if the appliance becomes more complex that the number of variables that control the appliances increases.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.64,0:11:04.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right now let's uh uh go back to the more broader kitchen tasks.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.70,0:11:07.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now we are facing an unknown environment.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.28,0:11:11.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh even though we can have a a manual for the uh for the for the appliance,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.68,0:11:14.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's more difficult to have a manual for the home and the robot will face
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.97,0:11:23.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,arbitrary objects unexpect uh different new object attributes and also the interaction uh of the objects.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.57,0:11:27.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,It may encounter unexpected failures as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.60,0:11:32.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now uh since the environment is new to the robots uh the robot needs to make hypothesis about
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.96,0:11:41.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,the world about objects about new predicates that describing the object attributes and also the action um effects.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.48,0:11:46.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now every time we make a hypothesis it could be true,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.22,0:11:55.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,false or simply unknown and the robot must verify whether the hypothesis uh is true or false actively through reasoning.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.02,0:12:04.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now uh in short uh what do we do is that internally we maintain a set of hypothesis whose whose uh veracity may be unknown.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.17,0:12:07.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have a scene graph and there is a system dynamics.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.25,0:12:12.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,The system dynamic controls that the out outcome of actions on the on the objects in
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.72,0:12:18.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,the in the world but also affects our belief on whether the hypothesis is true or not.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.72,0:12:23.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then we can uh then we want to derive the plan of actions for the robots.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.86,0:12:25.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,There are two approaches.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.66,0:12:35.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,One is again we can ask um the foundation model to predict the plan directly or alternatively uh we can do a search
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.40,0:12:43.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,in this case that we are going to encode the input into a PDDL format and do the Fast Downward.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.80,0:12:51.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now one challenge here is that PDDL planning is deterministic while our uh hypothesis are uncertain.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.20,0:12:56.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Therefore, we have to u perform a determinization trick in order to plan effectively.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.40,0:12:59.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Skipping some technical uh details.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.39,0:12:59.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,So,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.83,0:13:06.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,let's take a look at u the uh how our robot works this
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.41,0:13:12.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,time to heat up a chicken burger and put on the coffee table.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.40,0:13:18.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, it has to find the burger and make sure it is made of chicken.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.64,0:13:26.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it detects that maybe there is a burger on the on the on the table and have to take a look.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.24,0:13:28.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, unfortunately it's not made of chicken.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.24,0:13:32.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we have to regenerate that hypothesis and replan.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.04,0:13:35.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,But they have to put away this burger first.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.44,0:13:40.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then this time it discovers the kitchen and reasons that
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.32,0:13:50.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,the the the fridge the fridge may contain the burger.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.80,0:13:52.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Ah, this one it is a chicken burger.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.96,0:13:55.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.52,0:14:01.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Put it into the microwave.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.60,0:14:10.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,activate it to heat
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.12,0:14:17.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,it up until finally
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.33,0:14:19.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,it wants to u serve it on the table,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.02,0:14:20.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.43,0:14:22.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a very long horizon task.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.46,0:14:27.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,We tried on quite a variety of different kitchen and the living room and tasks.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.03,0:14:35.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the first one is kind of cute that it wants to turn off the living room light and just look at the control panel at the number of buttons on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.13,0:14:37.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,Even the human would have difficulty with that.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.77,0:14:41.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,So the robot has to try out and make hypothesis which one is the right one
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.90,0:14:46.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,until it turns it off and checks that in the living room that it's actually dark.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.69,0:14:50.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,We actually tried on different robots as well on the same with the same system.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.66,0:14:55.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this one's operating a microwave right now and uh and uh looking
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.52,0:14:58.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,for drinks and looking for a mug
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.33,0:15:10.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,with a smiley face on the fridge.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.24,0:15:12.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.08,0:15:12.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.56,0:15:15.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,Look at the performance a little bit more in closer details.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.29,0:15:18.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,that we systematically evaluated in two experimental setting.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.40,0:15:21.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,The first one is the blocks processing world.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.88,0:15:29.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's very similar to the classic blocks world but with an additional feature that we have a set of processors that can color or
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.52,0:15:38.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,texturize the blocks and uh and but the function of each of this processor is unknown to the robot in advance and therefore that
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.36,0:15:45.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,the robots to find out in order to to operate properly and the the goal is simply to achieve a configuration of blocks that
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.72,0:15:54.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,with the right kind of uh color and texture right and the other setting is the the well-known AI2 to thorough here are the results.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.09,0:15:59.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so there are three uh variants of this with no hypothesis being made.
