Dialogue: 0,1:04:45.28,1:04:45.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:45.64,1:04:47.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,So uh what is the motivation?
Dialogue: 0,1:04:47.44,1:04:56.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Motivation is that as we all know uh in robotics we have to deal with uncertainties and uncertainties can be in perception in modeling and so forth.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:56.40,1:04:59.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we focus mostly on modeling uncertainties.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:59.19,1:05:01.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,So a robot is a model of itself of the environment.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:01.75,1:05:08.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,This model is uncertain by construction then it has to do to deal with this uncertainty for taking decisions.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:08.09,1:05:08.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:08.54,1:05:14.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,So what are the possible approaches and in general people take or took in robotics.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:14.35,1:05:20.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you can uh try to have a fancy controller policy that is able to deal with uncertainty.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:20.22,1:05:27.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,The point here is that you can but this can be sometimes cumbersome or hard to implement and sometimes you don't want to do that.
