Dialogue: 0,1:05:28.00,1:05:32.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,the sense that sometimes you get a robot with has already a controller and that's it.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:32.50,1:05:33.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,You cannot change it.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:33.47,1:05:34.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,You have to work with what you have.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:34.87,1:05:37.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, so this is not always possible.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:37.08,1:05:43.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, then you may seek strong guarantees from the us of a specific policy or controller.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:43.06,1:05:49.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this the problem here is that many times it is possible if you simplify your model because so you're saying I want strong guarantees but then
Dialogue: 0,1:05:49.22,1:05:56.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,I have to use a simplified model and then your guarantees are not that strong you know in practice and also you have to invent many times something.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:56.27,1:06:03.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,like some quantities, some function, contraction metric and this is also not always possible then you want to compute
Dialogue: 0,1:06:03.12,1:06:10.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,computational feasibility and this again can be manageable only for simplified models okay and another point that I think many people
Dialogue: 0,1:06:10.94,1:06:19.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,take is to say my uncertainty is a generic perturbation like you know an additive process noise something like that this
Dialogue: 0,1:06:19.08,1:06:27.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,simplifies the math but then you don't have any structure and then your uncertainty prediction will be very very conservative Okay.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:27.10,1:06:33.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, so what we try to do, so we try to have a method which is um which has a general applicability.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:33.50,1:06:38.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that doesn't require any unnecessary simplification of the model of the robot.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:38.42,1:06:42.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Whatever it is, we can use it under some assumptions.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:42.72,1:06:44.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,An approach which is systematic.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:44.55,1:06:46.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,We don't have to invent anything at all.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:46.42,1:06:54.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,We take the model of the robot and we can apply our approach you know also in automized way which has a computational feasibility.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:54.44,1:06:57.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we don't have to resort to a full GPU cluster to run our stuff.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:58.00,1:06:58.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:58.53,1:07:02.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that exploits at most the structure of uncertainty.
