Dialogue: 0,1:08:42.50,1:08:44.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,So how to do this?
Dialogue: 0,1:08:44.51,1:08:52.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,We came up with this metric this sensitivity matrix which basically is the variation of the evolution of the state in closed loop.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:52.64,1:08:59.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,So for the robots and the controller against variations on the parameters evaluated at the nominal values.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:59.48,1:09:06.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this is a matrix that you can compute easily and it can be used as a metric a metric for optimization for generating motion plans.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:06.48,1:09:06.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:06.96,1:09:10.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it can be used as a robustness metric.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:10.19,1:09:15.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now this matrix doesn't have a close form but you can come up with a very easily with an OD
Dialogue: 0,1:09:15.87,1:09:22.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,a standard OD that you for propagate and again this the point here is that this step is completely systematic.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:22.89,1:09:29.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,This can always be done as long as you can compute the Jacobians of your robot dynamics and control.
